cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "bay-urban-flood-map: San Francisco Bay Area Urban Stormwater and Compound Sea Level Rise Flood Model"
version: "0.6.1"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/petermodracee/bay-urban-flood-map"
url: "https://bay-urban-flood-map.pages.dev"
authors:
  - family-names: "Modracee"
    given-names: "Peter"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-1210-9429"
abstract: >-
  An open-source, screening-level 2D urban stormwater and compound sea level rise
  flood model and serverless web viewer for the San Francisco Bay Area, built with
  HydroMT-SFINCS (20 m / 2 m subgrid terrain) and MapLibre GL JS with Cloud
  Optimized GeoTIFFs (COGs). Models heavy rainfall pooling in impervious urban
  basins under tidally constrained coastal boundary conditions across 10-year and
  100-year design rainfall paired with high tide and storm surge (coincident
  stress scenarios with undefined joint return period), 0 to +5 ft sea level rise
  increments, and historical atmospheric river hindcasts, validated against four
  open-data validation tiers plus a tide-boundary check.
keywords:
  - urban flooding
  - stormwater
  - sea level rise
  - compound flooding
  - SFINCS
  - HydroMT
  - San Francisco Bay Area
  - Cloud Optimized GeoTIFF
